  "notes": "{早|はや}く is the adverbial form of the i-adjective {早|はや}い. It covers three related meanings: early (time), quickly (speed), and soon (desire for something to happen).\n\nFORMATION:\n{早|はや}い → {早|はや}く (i-adjective → adverb by changing い to く)\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {早|はや}く: early or quickly (time-oriented — covers both meanings)\n- {速|はや}く: fast, at high speed (purely about speed)\nIn practice, {早|はや}く is used for both senses and is the more common spelling.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {早|はや}く{起|お}きる: to wake up early\n- {早|はや}く{帰|かえ}る: to go home early\n- できるだけ{早|はや}く: as soon as possible\n- {早|はや}く{元気|げんき}になってね: get well soon\n\nNOTE:\n{早|はや}く! on its own works as an urging expression: \"Hurry up!\"",
